nglamorous Game of the Century","description":"The Week 13 game will mark the first time since at least 2000 that two teams that are winless against FBS opponents will meet in their final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T01:19:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50587546/utep-niu-college-football-game-century","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana falls from 12-team field in 4th CFP rankings; Horns, Vols leap Bama","description":"Defending champ Indiana fell six spots to No. 14, while Alabama was leaped by Texas and Tennessee and fell out of the top five in the latest CFP rankings Tuesday night.","published":"2026-11-25T07:42:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588082/indiana-top-12-cfp-rankings-texas-tennessee-leap-alabama","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's fourth top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's fourth set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T02:02:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584328/cfp-2026-fourth-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU asks judge to throw out SEC's 'unwarranted' suit against Tigers","description":"LSU is asking a federal judge to dismiss the SEC's lawsuit against the Tigers, arguing that many of the plaintiffs in the case are protected by sovereign immunity as state officials and that the league doesn't have jurisdiction.","published":"2026-11-25T05:10:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588015/lsu-asks-judge-throw-sec-unwarranted-suit-tigers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Stanford quarterback Davis Warren returning in 2027","description":"Davis Warren has agreed to return to the Cardinal for his final year of eligibility, sources said.","published":"2026-11-25T01:32:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50588012/stanford-quarterback-davis-warren-returning-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wyoming's Jay Sawvel gets self-imposed 1-game ban over tampering violations","description":"Wyoming coach Jay Sawvel will serve a one-game suspension Saturday as part of the school's self-imposed penalties for impermissible contacting of players.","published":"2026-11-25T00:01:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50586972/wyoming-coach-jay-sawvel-gets-self-imposed-1-game-suspension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5065596/tavion-gadson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavion_Gadson"},"pick":{"pick":64,"round":2,"team":"SF","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Tavion Gadson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavion_Gadson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:34Z","intro":"Tavion Gadson is an American college football defensive tackle for the Kentucky Wildcats.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Gadson was born in Savannah, Georgia. He attended Jenkins High School in Savannah where as a senior, he was the Region 1-5A Defensive Player of the Year after recording 40 tackles and five sacks. He originally committed to play college football at Florida State University before flipping his commitment to the University of Kentucky."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Gadson played in four games his first year at Kentucky in 2023 and redshirted. In 2024, he played in only one game after suffering a knee injury during the spring. In 2025, Gadson played in 11 games with one start and had 28 tackles and 2.5 sacks. He returned to Kentucky in 2026."}]}}